 "deepDive": {
  "domain": "Law, courts & regulation",
  "title": "Courts, vetoes and orders: who gets the last word",
  "body": "**US.** The administration is using federal courts to shape how midterm votes are counted. In California, DOJ wants about 20,000 mail ballots from suspected noncitizens set aside; at the 25 Oct argument, Ninth Circuit judges doubted they had jurisdiction and suggested the Elections Clause leaves vote-counting to states ([Election Law Blog](https://electionlawblog.org/2026/ninth-circuit-panel-seems-skeptical-of-dojs-attempt-to-force-california-to-segregate-ballots-from-purported-noncitizens/)). In Alaska, DOJ seeks to block certification if Sen. Sullivan narrowly loses ([AP via Alaska Public Media](https://alaskapublic.org/news/politics/elections/2026-10-23/trumps-administration-sues-to-block-a-possible-democratic-win-in-the-alaska-u-s-senate-race)). Experts quoted by AP doubt the statutes allow either remedy, and the Purcell principle makes courts wary of late changes.\n\n**Poland.** The abortion bills passed on 20 Oct (233–203 and 217–213) would restore termination for severe foetal defects, reversing the 2020 Constitutional Tribunal ruling, and partly decriminalise helping with an abortion ([Polsat News](https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2026-10-25/dorota-loboda-o-zmianach-w-prawie-aborcyjnym-to-krok-do-przodu/)). President Nawrocki pledged not to sign any liberalisation, and the coalition lacks the three-fifths Sejm majority to override a veto. Analysis: the current rules are likely to stand until at least the 2027 election.\n\n**Kraków.** Mayor Gibała's order scrapping six City Hall departments removes a management layer created in 2025, but no one has yet said who supervises transport, roads and schools ([Radio Kraków](https://www.radiokrakow.pl/aktualnosci/krakow/szesc-departamentow-do-likwidacji-lukasz-gibala-podpisal-zarzadzenie)). His fare resolution and a 5 zł tourist fee need the council, where KO and Nowa Lewica hold the majority.\n\n**India.** Karnataka's prosecution sanction in the KPSC exam-leak case is the gateway, under the Prevention of Corruption Act, for the CID and ED to take a public servant to trial ([ANI](https://www.aninews.in/news/national/general-news/karnataka-cm-shivakumar-vows-to-give-kpsc-a-8216new-form8217-says-permission-granted-to-interrogate-accused-in-irregularities-case20261026013758)). The Supreme Court and eGazette could not be checked this run.",
  "links": [
   {
    "label": "Election Law Blog",
    "url": "https://electionlawblog.org/2026/ninth-circuit-panel-seems-skeptical-of-dojs-attempt-to-force-california-to-segregate-ballots-from-purported-noncitizens/"
   },
   {
    "label": "Polsat News",
    "url": "https://www.polsatnews.pl/wiadomosc/2026-10-25/dorota-loboda-o-zmianach-w-prawie-aborcyjnym-to-krok-do-przodu/"
   }
  ]
 },
